# 01 — Reliable UDP Communication in Mininet

## Objective
Build a UDP client-server application in Mininet and add basic reliability
using sequence numbers, ACKs, timeout, and retransmission (Stop-and-Wait),
then evaluate behaviour under 0%, 5%, and 10% simulated packet loss.

## Topology
```
h1 ---- s1 ---- h2      h1 = Server (10.0.0.1)      h2 = Client (10.0.0.2)
```

## Packet Formats
| Direction | Format | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Client -> Server | `SEQ\|MESSAGE` | `3\|Message 3 from h2` |
| Server -> Client | `ACK\|SEQ` | `ACK\|3` |

## Timeout Rule (derived from roll number's last digit)
| Last digit | Timeout |
|---|---|
| 0-1 | 0.5 s |
| 2-3 | 0.7 s |
| 4-5 | 1.0 s |
| 6-7 | 1.2 s |
| 8-9 | 1.5 s |

`client.py` computes this automatically from `--roll` — no manual editing needed.

