## How to Run (inside Mininet)

1. Start Mininet with the required loss condition (repeat for 0, 5, 10):
   ```bash
   sudo mn --link tc,bw=5,delay=30ms,loss=0
   ```
2. Verify the topology:
   ```
   mininet> nodes
   mininet> net
   mininet> pingall
   ```
   (screenshot each of these three commands)
3. Start the server on h1:
   ```
   mininet> h1 python3 server.py --port 5000 --expected 10 &
   ```
4. Run the client on h2, passing your own roll number/name and the loss
   percent that matches the `sudo mn` command you started with:
   ```
   mininet> h2 python3 client.py --server 10.0.0.1 --port 5000 \
                                  --roll <YOUR_ROLL_NO> --name "<YOUR NAME>" \
                                  --loss 0 --csv result_table.csv
   ```
5. Repeat steps 1–4 for `loss=5` and `loss=10`. `client.py` appends a new
   row to `result_table.csv` each run, so after three runs the file has
   exactly the 3 required data rows.
6. Screenshot the server and client terminal output for each run
   (`server_output.png`, `client_output.png`).

